@startuml
title udo — save(path): re-save the nearest file-owning container

actor TUI
participant Tree
participant Node
participant "persist\n(write_toml_atomic)" as Persist

TUI -> Tree : save(path)
Tree -> Tree : owner = nearest Container ancestor(path)\n(missing path -> Err)
Tree -> Node : ContainerData::from(container)\n(tasks = Task children,\n children = Container child dirs + unloaded)
Tree -> Persist : write <dir>/.udo.toml\n(root too: ~/.config/udo/.udo.toml)
Persist --> Tree : Ok
Tree --> TUI : Ok

note over Tree
  Editing a Task never writes its own file —
  it re-saves the parent container that owns it.
end note

@enduml
